      "dom_id": "step-q355000",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Mike wants to buy some pears. The price of pears in a nearby store is $$0.95/lb.$ How much would Mike pay for $5$ pounds of pears?",
      "worked_solution": "The unit price of pears is $$0.95/lb.$ To find the cost of $5$ pounds of pears, we multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.95\\times 5 & =4.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mike would pay $$4.75$ for $5$ pounds of pears.",
