    "q-91908": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91908",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Lucy wants to make a cake and is going to buy some fruit to decorate. How much would it cost her to buy $\\frac{1}{8}$ of a pound of strawberries?\n\n| Item | Price |\n| --- | --- |\n| Peach | $$1.75/\\text{lb}$ |\n| Strawberries | $$2.00/\\text{lb}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The unit price of strawberries is $$2.00/\\text{lb}.$ To find the cost of  $\\frac{1}{8}$ of a pound of strawberries, we multiply: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\times \\frac{1}{8} & =\\frac{2}{1}\\times \\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\times 1}{1\\times 8} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =2÷8 \\\\  & =0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it would cost Lucy $$0.25$ to buy $\\frac{1}{8}$ of a pound of strawberries.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
