      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Tom wants to buy some oranges. The price of oranges in a nearby store is $$0.75/lb.$ How much would Tom pay for $3$ pounds of oranges?",
      "worked_solution": "The unit price of oranges is $$0.75/lb.$ To find the cost of  $3$ pounds of oranges, we multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.75\\times 3 & =2.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Tom would pay  $$2.25$ for $3$ pounds of oranges.",
