    "q-355003": {
      "dom_id": "step-q355003",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Jenny is going to the craft store to buy some supplies. How much would it cost her to buy $\\frac{1}{2}$ of a yard of gold ribbon?\n\n| Item | Price |\n| --- | --- |\n| Gold Ribbon | $$5/\\text{yd}$ |\n| Silver Ribbon | $$4.5/\\text{yd}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The unit price of gold ribbon is $$5/\\text{yd}.$ To find the cost of  $\\frac{1}{2}$ of a yard of gold ribbon, we multiply: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\times \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{5}{1}\\times \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\times 1}{1\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =5÷2 \\\\  & =2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it would cost Jenny $$2.50$ to buy $\\frac{1}{2}$ of a yard of gold ribbon.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
