    "q-68895": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68895",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "At Chan's SuperMarket, there are three different bottles of spicy peach BBQ sauce:\n\n- The $17$-ounce $A$-brand bottle costs $$14.96\\,.$\n\n- The $19$-ounce $B$-brand bottle costs $$15.96\\,.$\n\n- The $18$-ounce $C$-brand bottle costs $$15.66\\,.$\n\nWhich brand of spicy peach BBQ sauce is the best deal?",
      "worked_solution": "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three brands. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of ounces.  \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in the $A$-brand bottle,  we get\n\n$$\n14.96÷17=0.88\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of the $A$-brand bottle is $$0.88.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in the $B$-brand bottle,  we get\n\n$$\n15.96÷19=0.84\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of the $B$-brand bottle is $$0.84.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in the $C$-brand bottle,  we get\n\n$$\n15.66÷18=0.87\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of the $C$-brand bottle is $$0.87.$\n\nFrom the above, we see that brand $B$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, brand $B$ is the best deal.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
