    "q-68939": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68939",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Sarah, a registered nurse, charges $$1.25$ per minute for her work in a rehabilitation center. How long should she work for $1$ dollar?",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$1.25$ per minute (dollars per minute). To find how many minutes Sarah should work  for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in minutes per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n1.25\\,\\text{dollars per minute}\\,\\to \\,1÷1.25=0.8\\,\\text{minutes per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.8$ minutes per dollar. Therefore, Sarah should work  $0.8$ minutes for $1$ dollar.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
