    "q-68507": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68507",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Mia charges $$0.20$ per minute for babysitting. For how long did she babysit if she earns $1$ dollar?",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$0.2$ per minute (dollars per minute). To find how many minutes she babysits for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in minutes per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n0.2\\,\\text{dollars per minute}\\,\\to \\,1÷0.2=5\\,\\text{minutes per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $5$ minutes per dollar. Therefore, Mia babysits $5$ minutes for $1$ dollar.",
