    "q-91919": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91919",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "At the vegetable market, the unit price for bananas is $$2.50$ per kilogram. How many kilograms of bananas can Mary buy with $$1?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$2.50$ per kilogram (dollars per kilogram). To find the number of kilograms of bananas that Mary can buy for $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in kilograms per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n2.50\\,\\text{dollars per kilogram}\\,\\to \\,1÷2.50=0.4\\,\\text{kilograms per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.4$ kilograms per dollar. Therefore, Mary can buy $0.4$ kilograms of bananas.",
